      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. so if the evidence really points toward density being a \"strategic necessity,\" does that basically mean that trying to preserve single-family neighborhoods is just an outdated way of thinking that cities should stop entertaining? like, is there even a legitimate policy case for it anymore, or is it just a hurdle that needs to be cleared?",
